---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

const base = '/participation-ces-classification/20261107-01/';
type Row = {
	dimension: string; group: string; respondents: number;
	record_positive_weight_fraction: number; classified_nonvote_weight_fraction: number;
	unresolved_weight_fraction: number; conditional_compatible_fraction: number[];
	effective_sample_size_not_design_precision: number;
};
const analysis: {
	rows: Row[];
	source_accounting: {
		native_respondents: number; postwave_respondents: number;
		missing_postwave_weight_nonresponse: number; selected_US50_postwave_respondents: number;
		DC_postwave_respondents_excluded_from_US50: number;
	};
	record_only_compatible_fraction_same_post_frame_overall_only: number[];
} = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}classification-evidence.json`, 'utf8'));
const integer = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US', { maximumFractionDigits: 0 });
const percent = (value: number) => `${(100 * value).toFixed(1)}%`;
const counts = analysis.source_accounting;
const dimensions = [
	['overall', 'Overall: 50-state adult post-wave sample',
		'The same 50-state post-wave frame used for every table below; D.C. is excluded.'],
	['calendar_year_age_2024', 'Age in calendar year 2024',
		'2024 minus documented birth year, not exact election-day age or a fixed 2026 age cohort.'],
	['education_2024', 'Source-reported education',
		'Native educational attainment, not neighborhood college share.'],
	['gender_2024', 'Survey-reported gender',
		'Native Man/Woman labels, not administrative sex. Non-binary and Other remain in overall totals.'],
	['race_education_2024', 'Combined race/ethnicity and education',
		'A native-derived joint partition, not a product of demographic marginals. College degree means 4-year or post-graduate.'],
	['race_ethnicity_2024', 'Combined race and Hispanic ethnicity',
		'Hispanic if either the native Hispanic-origin field is Yes or native race is Hispanic; otherwise non-Hispanic requires an explicit No to Hispanic origin.'],
	['source_race_2024', 'Native source race, kept separate',
		'The source race answer includes Hispanic as a category. It is not interchangeable with the combined race/ethnicity table or SSRS categories.'],
];
---

<section id="participation-ces-classification" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="ces-classification-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Historical participation evidence · 2024 Cooperative Election Study</p>
		<h2 id="ces-classification-title">Keep unresolved voting histories in the denominator</h2>
		<p>These selected national demographic tables describe <strong>2024 participation classifications</strong>
			in an adult survey sample. They are not population-turnout point estimates or evidence of
			2026 switching, staying home or first-time voting.</p>
	</header>
	<p data-ces-response-accounting>{`Of ${integer(counts.native_respondents)} source respondents, ${integer(counts.postwave_respondents)} have post-wave weights; ${integer(counts.missing_postwave_weight_nonresponse)} without those weights remain in source nonresponse accounting. These tables retain ${integer(counts.selected_US50_postwave_respondents)} respondents across the 50 states and exclude ${integer(counts.DC_postwave_respondents_excluded_from_US50)} D.C. respondents. Sample counts are not population totals or an eligible-voter denominator.`}</p>
	<p><strong>All unresolved histories stay in the full group denominator.</strong> The conditional
		range lets unresolved histories be either votes or nonvotes, assuming the known classifications
		are correct. It is <strong>not a confidence interval</strong> and does not cover matching,
		reporting, nonresponse or calibration errors. Differences between groups are not significance tests.</p>
	{dimensions.map(([dimension, label, definition]) => <details class="explorer-notes" open={dimension === 'overall'} data-ces-table={dimension}>
		<summary>{label}</summary>
		<p>{definition}</p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${label}: conditional participation classification`}>
			<table>
				<caption>Weighted fractions of the full selected group, including unresolved histories.
					Raw and Kish sample sizes are support diagnostics, not design precision.</caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Group</th><th scope="col">Raw respondents</th>
					<th scope="col">Recorded vote</th><th scope="col">Classified nonvote</th>
					<th scope="col">Unresolved</th><th scope="col">Conditional compatible fraction</th>
					<th scope="col">Kish diagnostic</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>{analysis.rows.filter(row => row.dimension === dimension).map(row => <tr
					data-ces-row data-ces-dimension={dimension} data-ces-group={row.group}>
					<th scope="row">{dimension === 'overall' ? '50-state sample' : row.group}</th>
					<td data-ces-value="respondents">{integer(row.respondents)}</td>
					<td data-ces-value="record_positive_weight_fraction">{percent(row.record_positive_weight_fraction)}</td>
					<td data-ces-value="classified_nonvote_weight_fraction">{percent(row.classified_nonvote_weight_fraction)}</td>
					<td data-ces-value="unresolved_weight_fraction">{percent(row.unresolved_weight_fraction)}</td>
					<td><span data-ces-value="lower">{percent(row.conditional_compatible_fraction[0])}</span>
						{' to '}<span data-ces-value="upper">{percent(row.conditional_compatible_fraction[1])}</span></td>
					<td data-ces-value="effective_sample_size_not_design_precision">{integer(row.effective_sample_size_not_design_precision)}</td>
				</tr>)}</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</details>)}
	<p><strong>Nonexhaustive, overlapping demographic views.</strong> Groups omitted together for
		disclosure protection remain in overall totals, not zero or missing-as-nonvote.
		Do not add tables across dimensions. Income, urban/suburban/rural residence and additional
		intersections are not qualified here. All 51 state/D.C. withholding dispositions remain
		in the complete output; national rows are not allocated to states, counties or precincts.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes" data-ces-methods>
		<summary>Classification assumptions, source limitations and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>Recorded votes and explicit recorded nonvotes take precedence over self-reports.
			Unmatched self-reported nonregistration/nonvoting can classify a nonvote.
			Unmatched reported voters, missing histories and contradictory unmatched reports remain
			unresolved in this conservative conflict-as-unknown specification.</p>
		<p>With full weight <code>W = P + N + U</code>, recorded-vote weight P, classified-nonvote
			weight N and unresolved weight U, the range is <code>[P/W, (P+U)/W]</code>.
			Using <code>P/(P+N)</code> would improperly remove unresolved respondents.
			Only positive <code>commonpostweight</code> is used; adult, matched-active-registered and
			validated-voter weight frames are not pooled.</p>
		<p>Using only recorded nonvotes in this exact same post-wave frame gives an overall-only
			comparator of <span data-ces-comparator="lower">{percent(analysis.record_only_compatible_fraction_same_post_frame_overall_only[0])}</span>
			{' to '}<span data-ces-comparator="upper">{percent(analysis.record_only_compatible_fraction_same_post_frame_overall_only[1])}</span>.
			It is not a second population-turnout estimate or another demographic table.</p>
		<p>Validation uses active matched registration in June-July 2025, not a demonstrated
			election-day eligible population or continuing residence. Utah private/withheld records
			can limit matching. Truthful reported nonparticipation and correct validation are
			assumptions. Unknowns, changing attributes, nonresponse and calibration limitations remain.
			Neither raw support nor Kish weight concentration establishes anonymity or design precision.</p>
		<p>The complete selected aggregates, native CSV/guide receipts, relevant native numeric-label
			definitions, methodology, calculations, exact code, tests and results reproduce offline.
			This does not recreate private respondent extraction or independently validate individual
			histories. Original native respondent files, fine cells, private audits, joins and scores
			are not redistributed. The source CSV does not supply 2020/2022 histories; these are not
			a longitudinal panel across those elections.</p>
		<p>Source: <a href="https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/X11EP6">2024 Cooperative Election Study, Common Content</a>,
			Harvard Dataverse release 9.0, CC0 1.0. Independent analysis, not endorsed by the study.
			The full Stata respondent file was not downloaded or hash verified; bounded metadata
			receipts are distinct from the original CSV and guide receipts.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete selected classification analysis + inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}classification-evidence.json`} download>Classification fractions + all state/D.C. dispositions (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Classification archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-ces-classification { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
	.table-wrap { max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; }
	table { width: 100%; min-width: 50rem; }
	td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
</style>
